Republican senator Susan Collins  remembers mr. Bush as a compassionate  leader Collins became close friends with  the former president and first lady more  than 20 years ago back in 1994 when I  was running for governor of Maine I had  just won an eight-way Republican primary  and I got a call from President and mrs.  Bush inviting me to have lunch with them  at Kennebunkport at walkers point well  you can imagine how absolutely thrilled  that I was and they were always so kind  to me my hope is that people will  reflect on his legacy on his grace his  dignity on his accomplishments and that  it will inspire people to try to find  common ground and to put an end to the  polarization and divisiveness that is so  terrible for our country and for our  government right now and Collins says  she was touched that the former  president's final tweet praised her  courage and her leadership and John as  much as the president loved Maine you  can't overstate how much he loved the  city of Houston he moved here in 1959  alongside his young family and he was  interviewed by a local reporter a few  years back and was asked do you consider  yourself a Houstonian to which he  replied I don't want to be less than  kind but that's a dumb question where he  made his place in the world he had many  friends in Houston Connecticut  Washington Maine and the country today  bianna thank you
 

